C WW
"Lahav & Boker, TOPLAS 2022, Ex. 3.7 (WW). Two threads each write x and then read
 it, and each reads the OTHER thread's value. Both writes are hb|loc-unrelated, so
 WRA's weak-read-coherence -- which uses hb|loc rather than mo to decide which of
 two writes to a location is the later -- has nothing to fire on, and WRA ALLOWS
 the outcome. RA and SRA order the two writes by mo, so whichever is mo-earlier is
 read by a thread aware of the mo-later one, violating read-coherence: both FORBID
 it. This is WRA failing SC-per-location on a single-location program."
{ }
P0 (atomic_int* x) {
  atomic_store_explicit(x,1,memory_order_release);
  int r0 = atomic_load_explicit(x,memory_order_acquire);
}
P1 (atomic_int* x) {
  atomic_store_explicit(x,2,memory_order_release);
  int r1 = atomic_load_explicit(x,memory_order_acquire);
}
exists (0:r0=2 /\ 1:r1=1)
